def is_prime(n: int) -> bool:
    if n < 2:
        return False
    if n == 2:
        return True
    if n % 2 == 0:
        return False
    for i in range(3, int(n**0.5) + 1, 2):
        if n % i == 0:
            return False
    return True
```

This function checks whether a number `n` is prime by testing divisibility only up to the square root of `n`. It handles edge cases (numbers less than 2, even numbers) and only checks odd divisors, reducing the number of iterations. The time complexity is O(sqrt(n)) and the space complexity is O(1).

